{"title":"2016 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the area of the shaded region.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95f8b885091c3cb0d7a2cb9325def6a059bfb982.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  size(6cm); defaultpen(fontsize(9pt)); draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,5)--(0,5)--cycle); filldraw((7,0)--(8,0)--(8,1)--(0,4)--(0,5)--(1,5)--cycle,gray(0.8));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(1/2,5),dir(90)); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,(9/2,5),dir(90));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(8,1/2),dir(0)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(8,3),dir(0));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(15/2,0),dir(270)); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,(7/2,0),dir(270));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(0,9/2),dir(180)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(0,2),dir(180));  [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"195\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48df8e12829ad0630bd6550487fcf1bd20fbe004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4\\dfrac{3}{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 5\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 5\\dfrac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\dfrac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"388\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60eda23e098229c26f4a92a2422e53765c97836.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  size(6cm); defaultpen(fontsize(9pt)); draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,5)--(0,5)--cycle); filldraw((7,0)--(8,0)--(8,1)--(0,4)--(0,5)--(1,5)--cycle,gray(0.8));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(1/2,5),dir(90)); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,(9/2,5),dir(90));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(8,1/2),dir(0));   label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(15/2,0),dir(270)); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,(7/2,0),dir(270));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(0,9/2),dir(180)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(0,2),dir(180));  draw((0,5)--(8,0));  [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"195\" />\n</p><p>The bases of these triangles are all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and by symmetry, their heights are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3adf28c1ab96fc4eddaa890ec574e4cea2caea36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3adf28c1ab96fc4eddaa890ec574e4cea2caea36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, their areas are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3628e955d7e4a0e6322ada48bc33c003f9b25dbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3628e955d7e4a0e6322ada48bc33c003f9b25dbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />, which add to the area of the shaded region, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f58dc126f0e3d6efbd6c22cbefc03fd6f3c857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{6\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"34\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the area of the unshaded area by calculating the area of the triangles and rectangles outside of the shaded region. We can do this by splitting up the unshaded areas into various triangles and rectangles as shown.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82cdaaa75ab582149da4c5e56880faabde9f14bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  size(6cm); defaultpen(fontsize(9pt)); draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,5)--(0,5)--cycle); filldraw((7,0)--(8,0)--(8,1)--(0,4)--(0,5)--(1,5)--cycle,gray(0.8));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(1/2,5),dir(90)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(6,5),dir(90)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(5/2,5),dir(90));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(8,1/2),dir(0)); label(&quot;$5/2$&quot;,(8,15/4),dir(0)); label(&quot;$3/2$&quot;,(8,7/4),dir(0));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(15/2,0),dir(270)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(2,0),dir(270)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(11/2,0),dir(270));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(0,9/2),dir(180)); label(&quot;$5/2$&quot;,(0,5/4),dir(180)); label(&quot;$3/2$&quot;,(0,13/4),dir(180));  draw((0,5/2)--(8,5/2)); draw((4,0)--(4,5));  [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"175\" />\n</p><p>Notice that the two added lines bisect each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides of the large rectangle.\n</p><p>Subtracting the unshaded area from the total area gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9db7a808fd496c8735e685fa235af98470f68e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40-33\\frac{1}{2}=\\boxed{6\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"129\" height=\"48\" />, so the correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that we can graph this on the coordinate plane.\n</p><p>The top-left shaded figure has coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524b999081f085cddf4ae0cb50e3ae017fe4c48e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,5), (0,5), (0,4), \\left(4,\\frac{5}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"204\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that we can apply the shoelace method to find the area of this polygon.\n</p><p>We find that the area of the polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f926e78edb1fc7bf25a7ec0b08bc93b33145c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>However, notice that the two shaded regions are two congruent polygons.\n</p><p>Hence, the total area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c39b511dbe55ed5cde4c8bf59ed84141cdc8d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13}{2}\\implies \\boxed{6\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"105\" height=\"48\" />  or  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b6192c64c68e3231dc8068e13b8c72669f681e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  size(6cm); defaultpen(fontsize(9pt)); draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,5)--(0,5)--cycle); filldraw((7,0)--(8,0)--(0,5)--(1,5)--cycle,gray(0.7)); filldraw((8,0)--(8,1)--(0,4)--(0,5)--cycle,gray(0.9));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(1/2,5),dir(90)); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,(9/2,5),dir(90));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(8,1/2),dir(0));   label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(15/2,0),dir(270)); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,(7/2,0),dir(270));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(0,9/2),dir(180)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(0,2),dir(180));  [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"195\" />\n</p><p>Split the region into four parts by the diagonal from the top left to the bottom right. Slide the top and bottom pieces next to each other to form a parallelogram with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3adf28c1ab96fc4eddaa890ec574e4cea2caea36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, and slide the left and right pieces next to each other to form a parallelogram with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09e35b79099fc525d6865f4330b99868d813ade1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. The total area is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038026a5d54b25d626aeb9734ff44c8cb03250d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot\\frac{5}{2}+1\\cdot\\frac{8}{2} = \\frac{(5+8)(1)}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"293\" height=\"49\" />. ~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Emerald_block\" title=\"User:Emerald block\">emerald_block</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb39ef68c092bd1a44e629723aac9cd271369bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  size(6cm); defaultpen(fontsize(9pt)); draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,5)--(0,5)--cycle); filldraw((7,0)--(8,0)--(8,1)--(0,4)--(0,5)--(1,5)--cycle,gray(0.8)); filldraw((1,0)--(0,0)--(0,1)--(8,4)--(8,5)--(7,5)--cycle,gray(0.8)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(1/2,5),dir(90)); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,(4,5),dir(90)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(15/2,5),dir(90)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(8,1/2),dir(0)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(8,5/2),dir(0)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(8,9/2),dir(0)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(15/2,0),dir(270)); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,(4,0),dir(270)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(1/2,0),dir(270)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(0,9/2),dir(180)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(0,5/2),dir(180)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(0,1/2),dir(180)); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"195\" />\n</p><p>We can subtract the 4 triangular areas from the overall rectangle. It can be noticed that two triangles have area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5efd5ec500dbcb682b034fae3b1b97a87213eb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6 \\cdot \\frac{5}{2}}{2} = \\frac{15}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"42\" />, and the other two triangles have area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822789bd1846659a55b1be0a84a200a70268db9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 \\cdot \\frac{8}{2}}{2} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"42\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/843622567e12d686e4e2f94ddfcb444e8ecde0d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"9\" /> the shaded area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5def12cad1dd413f666974ca9688264d9f0ec6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8 \\cdot 5) - 2(\\frac{15}{2}) - 2(6) = 40 - 15 - 12 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"335\" height=\"38\" />. Since the desired area is half the shaded region, our area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e1733166ccf16d5b51d5dd90ecb4c803e2e60705.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Champion1234\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Calculus)\">Solution 6 (Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the area before and after the intersection is the same, so we can just consider the area before the intersection and double it to get the total area of the shaded region.\n</p><p>There are two linear lines that can be labeled. The first intersects the side of length 5; By letting the bottom left side of the triangle be defined as (0,0), its slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e272f33e4d3b25a8180477f5c89b5f4356274aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{1-4}{8-0} = -\\frac{3}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"138\" height=\"40\" />. Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892f84de1eb5f50b8bf862eb415104c86d39277d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ y_1 = -\\frac{3}{8}x + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/3/053355b2b53d50795130638b4688d2062dee4f85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ y_1(0) = b = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"26\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b77fff3be5f87f3355ba88b3028f2dee09931fb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ y_1 = -\\frac{3}{8}x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>The second line's equation can be found in a similar fashion. Its slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dd430ae7258b74f02151e386ba8dbc4a139169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{0-5}{7-1} = -\\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"138\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b996b1fcd2a42c413d2c82f9d82984245ad445f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ y_2 = -\\frac{5}{6}x + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608fbee4e093e229472e1a00d16c2835d66ba575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ y_2(7) = -\\frac{35}{6} + b = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc0db8b70958509c306fb3fed0c0cf9ae8f1ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ b = \\frac{35}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f7100692809963180c5ce1833ebab2bda9018fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ y_2 = -\\frac{5}{6}x + \\frac{35}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Now we can take the area between lines. One thing to note is that we have to start at the point (1,5) because the rest of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0320ab2ddd4939f9072e5316fe8888b0cddee319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> is outside of the rectangle.\n</p><p>The area of the remaining shaded part from [0,1) can also be found using an integral. Assume the top side of the rectangle is defined as y = 5. We can find the area between the lines by integrating the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c62fe5fd505a3e48d4534a86a3e40621baef9fb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 - y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Now where do the lines meet? \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb9ab5acc3d3aa64a688952218e4547ce50ee4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ y_1 = y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"25\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8989b0dc49717548ccc7eb9d875c0e4350087725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ -\\frac{3}{8}x + 4 = -\\frac{5}{6}x + \\frac{35}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"40\" />\nSolving for x yields 4, so the graphs intersect at x = 4.\n</p><p>Now we can integrate.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/257528b46a4a4e07a8a7440ad83cd544fecac3e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Area_{shaded} = 2Area_{[0,1)} + 2Area_{(1,4]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"284\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee060001c9741dc7e6fd39b1a398d4c1d2d417a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2Area_{[0,1)} = 2\\int_0^1 5 - (-\\frac{3}{8}x + 4) dx \\\\ = 2\\int_0^1 1 + \\frac{3}{8}x dx = 2(x + \\frac{3}{16}x^2) \\left.\\right|_{\\;0}^{\\;1} \\\\ = 2(1 + \\frac{3}{16}1^2) = 2\\frac{19}{16} = \\frac{19}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"129\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b68abb897b43df06afc7d8afb96e8ac21847aaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\ 2Area_{(1,4]} = 2\\int_1^4 y_2 - y_1 dx = 2\\int_1^4 (-\\frac{5}{6}x + \\frac{35}{6}) - (-\\frac{3}{8}x + 4) dx \\\\ = 2\\int_1^4 (-\\frac{5}{6} + \\frac{3}{8})x + \\frac{35}{6} - 4 dx \\\\ = 2\\int_1^4 -\\frac{11}{24}x + \\frac{11}{6} dx = 2(-\\frac{11}{48}x^2 + \\frac{11}{6}x)\\left.\\right|_{\\;1}^{\\;4} \\\\ = 2((-\\frac{11}{48}4^2 + \\frac{11}{6}4) - (-\\frac{11}{48}1^2 + \\frac{11}{6}1)) = 2\\frac{33}{16} = \\frac{33}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"176\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54095caa5189fd46cc8bf9d9a8a0fdc3912f73d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Area_{shaded} = 2Area_{[0,1)} + 2Area_{(1,4]} = \\frac{19}{8} + \\frac{33}{8} = \\frac{19+33}{8} = \\frac{52}{8} = \\frac{13}{2} = 6.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"602\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e1733166ccf16d5b51d5dd90ecb4c803e2e60705.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~juicefruit\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/uxgX8h5fWrs\">https://youtu.be/uxgX8h5fWrs</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dHY8gjoYFXU\">https://youtu.be/dHY8gjoYFXU</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WojyKGOEk_g\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WojyKGOEk_g</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4_x1sgcQCp4?t=652\">https://youtu.be/4_x1sgcQCp4?t=652</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; fon